{{also|coïncide|coïncidé}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱh₂d-}}
From {{der|en|fr|coïncider}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|coincidere}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|coincidō}}, from {{m|la|co-}} + {{m|la|incidō}}, from {{m|la|in-}} + {{m|la|cadō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˌkoʊɪnˈsaɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-coincide.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪd}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To occupy exactly the same [[space]].
#: ''The two squares '''coincide''' nicely.''
# To occur at the same time.
#: ''The conference will '''coincide''' with his vacation.''
# To [[correspond]], [[concur]], or [[agree]].
#: ''Our ideas '''coincide''', except in certain areas.''

